From 5bf442dc4907d36f91796a60a6e229fefa2643b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 12:44:46 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] wmaker: choose the monitor of the Dock

With several monitors the Dock could only sit on the left or right edge
of the whole screen (or of the primary monitor with
KeepDockOnPrimaryHead), and dragging it towards another monitor only
flipped it between the two outer edges.

The Dock now has a monitor, kept in its state as "Monitor" in WMState:
"primary", the RandR connector name of an output ("HDMI-A-0", which
does not change when the outputs are reordered) or, without RandR, the
number of a Xinerama head. It is chosen

  - in the new "Monitor" submenu of the Dock menu, rebuilt each time it
    opens from the monitors connected at that moment (the primary one
    marked with "*"), plus "Edge of the whole screen" for the classic
    behaviour, which stays the default;
  - by dragging the Dock into another monitor: it goes to the side of
    that monitor nearest to the pointer.

A chosen monitor that is not connected sends the Dock to the primary
one without forgetting the choice (the menu lists it as
"(disconnected)"); when RandR reports it again the Dock goes back.
wRandR_Update() calls the new wDockUpdateHead(), which also keeps the
first icon inside the height of the monitor (monitors of different
heights). The choice is saved right away, so it survives a crash.

The drawers follow the Dock, as they already did for side changes.
